# Rust Type System and Serialization

Lux provides a type mapping and serialization layer between Elixir and Rust, enabling seamless data exchange and complex type definitions.

## Overview

The Rust integration consists of three core modules:

- **`Lux.Rust.TypeMapper`** - Advanced type mapping, struct/enum schemas, Serde integration, bidirectional encoding/decoding
- **`Lux.Rust.SerdeField`** - Field-level Serde metadata handling (rename, default, skip, tag/content)
- **`Lux.Rust`** - Centralized entry point with delegation to TypeMapper and SerdeField

## Type Mapping

### Primitive Types

Map Elixir atoms to Rust type strings:

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:integer)
# => {:ok, "i64"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:float)
# => {:ok, "f64"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:string)
# => {:ok, "String"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:boolean)
# => {:ok, "bool"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:bytes)
# => {:ok, "Vec<u8>"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.elixir_to_rust_type(:char)
# => {:ok, "char"}
```

Reverse mapping from Rust to Elixir:

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_to_elixir_type("i64")
# => {:ok, :integer}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_to_elixir_type("Option<String>")
# => {:ok, :option}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_to_elixir_type("HashMap<String, i64>")
# => {:ok, :hash_map}
```

### Container Types

```elixir
# Vec<T>
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.container_to_rust(:vec, {:primitive, :integer})
# => {:ok, "Vec<i64>"}

# Option<T>
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.container_to_rust(:option, {:primitive, :string})
# => {:ok, "Option<String>"}

# HashMap<K, V>
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.container_to_rust(:hash_map, {:primitive, :string})
# => {:ok, "HashMap<String, String>"}
```

### Type Descriptor Serialization

Serialize/deserialize complex type descriptors:

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.serialize_type({:container, :vec, {:primitive, :float}})
# => {:ok, "Vec<f64>"}

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.deserialize_type("Vec<Option<i64>>")
# => {:ok, {:container, :vec, {:container, :option, {:primitive, :integer}}}}
```

## Struct Schemas

Define Rust-compatible struct schemas with Serde metadata:

```elixir
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.struct_schema("TradeRequest", [
  {:symbol, :string, [rename: :snake_case]},
  {:price_usd, :float, [default: 0.0]},
  {:quantity, :integer, []}
])
```

Generate the corresponding Rust code:

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_definition(schema)
# => {:ok, "#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug)]\npub struct TradeRequest {\n    pub price_usd: f64,\n    pub quantity: i64,\n    pub symbol: String,\n}"}
```

### Struct Schemas with Serde Attributes

```elixir
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.serde_struct_schema(
  "Position",
  [
    {:side, :string, []},
    {:size, :float, []}
  ],
  tag: "type",
  content: "data"
)

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_definition(schema)
# => {:ok, "#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug)]\n#[serde(tag = \"type\", content = \"data\")]\npub struct Position {\n    pub side: String,\n    pub size: f64,\n}"}
```

## Enum Schemas

Define Rust-compatible enum schemas:

```elixir
# Unit variants
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.enum_schema("OrderSide", [:buy, :sell])

# Tuple variants
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.enum_schema("MarketEvent", [
  {:price_update, {:primitive, :float}},
  {:volume_change, {:primitive, :integer}},
  :shutdown
])

# With Serde attributes
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.serde_enum_schema(
  "TradeSignal",
  [:bullish, :bearish, :neutral],
  tag: "kind"
)
```

Generate Rust code:

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_definition(schema)
# => {:ok, "#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug)]\npub enum OrderSide {\n    Buy,\n    Sell,\n}"}
```

## Bidirectional Conversion

### Encoding (Elixir to Rust Wire Format)

```elixir
schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.struct_schema("Trade", [
  {:symbol, :string, []},
  {:price_usd, :float, [default: 0.0]}
])

Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.encode(%{symbol: "BTC/USD"}, schema)
# => {:ok, %{"symbol" => "BTC/USD", "price_usd" => 0.0}}
```

### Decoding (Rust Wire Format to Elixir)

```elixir
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.decode(%{"symbol" => "BTC/USD", "price_usd" => 50000.0}, schema)
# => {:ok, %{symbol: "BTC/USD", price_usd: 50000.0}}
```

## Type Manifests

Collect multiple schemas into a single manifest for code generation:

```elixir
trade_schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.struct_schema("Trade", [
  {:symbol, :string, []},
  {:amount, :float, []}
])

status_enum = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.enum_schema("Status", [:pending, :done])

manifest = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.manifest([trade_schema], [status_enum])

# Access generated Rust code
manifest[:rust_code]
# => "// Auto-generated Rust type definitions..."

# Access individual schemas
manifest[:structs]  # => [trade_schema]
manifest[:enums]    # => [status_enum]
```

## Serde Field Metadata

Fine-grained control over individual field serialization:

```elixir
# Rename a field for Serde
field = Lux.Rust.SerdeField.from_descriptor({
  :price_usd,
  :float,
  [rename: :snake_case, default: 0.0]
})

Lux.Rust.SerdeField.rust_name(field)  # => "price_usd"
Lux.Rust.SerdeField.elixir_name(field)  # => :price_usd

# Generate Rust field definition
Lux.Rust.SerdeField.to_rust_field(field)
# => "#[serde(default = \"0.0\")]\npub price_usd: f64,"
```

Supported Serde attributes:

| Attribute | Description | Example |
|-----------|-------------|---------|
| `:rename` | Rename field in Serde | `[rename: :snake_case]` |
| `:rename_all` | Rename all fields with a rule | `[rename_all: :PascalCase]` |
| `:default` | Default value | `[default: 0.0]` |
| `:tag` | Internally tagged enum | `[tag: "type"]` |
| `:content` | Adjacently tagged enum | `[content: "data"]` |
| `:skip_serializing_if` | Skip when condition met | `[skip_serializing_if: "is_none"]` |
| `:skip_deserializing` | Skip deserialization | `[skip_deserializing: true]` |

## Examples

### Complex Type Conversion

```elixir
# Define a complex struct with nested types
order_schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.struct_schema("Order", [
  {:order_id, :string, [rename: :snake_case]},
  {:side, :string, []},
  {:price, :float, [default: 0.0]},
  {:quantity, :integer, []},
  {:tags, :vec, [type_inner: :string]}
])

# Generate Rust code
{:ok, rust_code} = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_definition(order_schema)

# Encode Elixir data
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.encode(%{order_id: "ORD-001", side: "buy", quantity: 100}, order_schema)
# => {:ok, %{"order_id" => "ORD-001", "side" => "buy", "quantity" => 100}}

# Decode back
Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.decode(%{"order_id" => "ORD-001", "side" => "buy", "quantity" => 100}, order_schema)
# => {:ok, %{order_id: "ORD-001", side: "buy", quantity: 100}}
```

### Enum with Tagged Variants

```elixir
event_schema = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.serde_enum_schema(
  "ExchangeEvent",
  [
    :connected,
    :disconnected,
    {:trade, {:primitive, :string}},
    {:error, {:primitive, :string}}
  ],
  tag: "event_type"
)

{:ok, code} = Lux.Rust.TypeMapper.rust_definition(event_schema)
# Generates:
# #[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug)]
# #[serde(tag = "event_type")]
# pub enum ExchangeEvent {
#     Connected,
#     Disconnected,
#     Trade(String),
#     Error(String),
# }
```
